{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/642448-playable-pijavica-clan-how-to-do-it","id":642448,"title":"Playable Pijavica Clan; how to do it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-27T20:24:20-07:00","id":642448,"title":"Playable Pijavica Clan; how to do it?","content":"So, yeah, the title sums it up pretty well. The pijavica clan from the Lost Clans segment of the Shadows &amp; Blood corebook sounds really interesting, and we've seen some bloodlines with thematically appropriate powers in 1e (Phagia and the ability to feed through the skin, Siktri Pata's Yama's Benefice, which allows a vampire to become a living mass of blood). I'd be really interested in seeing how people think that this clan could be given viable stats for playing in a 2e game.<br /> <br /> After all, there is always the option of historical games, and even their fluff in the corebook gives a hook taht there may still be pijavicas haunting the nights without the rest of the Damned knowing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T03:36:58-07:00","id":642808,"title":"","content":"I know I would make their clan curse something along the lines of having to pay 1 more Vitae each night per dot of Humanity below 7 (minimum 1 more once the curse gets in effect) to keep their human appearance, or else the revert to the blob stage.<br /> <br /> As for Disciplines, maybe Protean, Resilience and either Obfuscate or Vigor (or both if you ditch Protean)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 08-28-2015, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:09:47-07:00","id":642995,"title":"","content":"GnomishAmerican did do a write-up of the Clan that's listed in the homebrew sticky. I'm not good enough to judge quality, but it's worth looking into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T02:02:05-08:00","id":835644,"title":"","content":"I just remembered this old topic, and I wanted to share a thought I had. What if I went with the idea that the clan &quot;boon&quot; for these vampires is the ability to assume a blood-based blob-form, borrowing mechanical inspiration from Yama's Benefice, with the clan bane of halving Humanity to determine damage from Banes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}